Z||000007||Patrick's Dad||05-25-2000||11:24 PM||||I'd be interested in following/corresponding on this. My car just came off the road (I know that the warm weather is just beginning, but now I have two kids and only one passenger seat....), and I'm planning on similar stuff. My list goes something like this:<P>New engine (Supercharged 3.4 is currently the front runner)<BR>Suspension upgrade; poly bushings all around, Konis, springs, etc.<BR>Brake upgrades; probably 10½" cross drilled rotors, maybe 11"s inside 16" five spokes. Just read in Kit car about new Aluminum calipers that reduce unsprung weight by nine pounds (per wheel, I think). Proportioning valve in the cockpit.<BR>Stereo: 350 watt MacIntosh/MbQuart system. Not a boomer. I like my classical and jazz too much. Yes, I listen to Creed and old Funk, too, but when I want to hear a piano, I want it to sound like a piano is in the car with me....<BR>Oh, by the way, no A/C<BR>Vented hood, side scoops (The right one will probably feed an oil cooler), and I haven't decided on the stock (style) spoiler (I've had two stolen. Grr.) or something that bonds flat to the decklid, like the IMSA, I think.<P>Maybe an off center stripe, but I haven't decided on that, either.||||reg||1
